window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-ayanokouji-atsuomi"]=[{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p55-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka matsuo chabashira-sae ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi ch 3  the drop out demand sits opposite the sweating principal in the office  delivers the prepared drop out papers and the matsuo leverage   how about you take a seat  i came all the way here to meet with you  after all   friends  don t make me laugh  there s no way you re capable of making friends   then i assume you re going to do as i say  no need to discuss anything  i m busy anyway   i ve prepared the documents necessary for you to drop out  i spoke to the principal about it  all i need is for you to say yes   for you  that might be true  but i have my own reasons   parent  you ve never recognized me as your parent before   the fact is that you ve been behaving selfishly  i ordered you to remain on standby   you re my property  a man may do as he wishes with his property  whether i keep you alive or kill you is up to me   don t you wonder how matsuo s doing  the person who told you about this school and gave you the idea to enroll   i hired him to manage you for a year in his capacity as a butler  but he chose to go against his employer   an outrageous  unforgiveable act  naturally  matsuo had to be punished   you can probably guess what i m about to say   but now he s been expelled   matsuo s son was strong  even though he was expelled from the school on which he d pinned his hopes  his determination didn t fade  he   bounced back and immediately tried to enroll in other schools  i did whatever was necessary to crush his attempts to advance  i made him give up  i did the same to matsuo  too  i tarnished his reputation  leaving him unable to find a job  his son also lost his way  and is now unemployed   he begged me to leave the boy alone  and committed suicide last month by self immolation   right now  his son s working part time  earning enough to live on and nothing else  with no guarantee of a future  no dreams  no hope  his family s tragedy is your fault  the boy must surely bear a deep grudge against you  even in death  he won t forgive you   the man who took care of you  who saved you  has died  and you show no reaction whatsoever  if matsuo could see you now  he d be full of regret   matsuo s death has already been recorded  if necessary  i can send for the papers confirming it   you ve changed quite a bit  kiyotaka   what happened that year  what made you so determined to go to this school   i don t entirely understand  but it seems that i have no choice but to accept  i suppose that temporarily suspending the facility s activity was a mistake  to think that a plan sixteen years in the making could be ruined in just a year   i understand why you re here   but if you think the matter is settled  you re naive  as with matsuo s son  i can force you to quit   that s a statement made without proof   there s no need to bring a bodyguard along to visit a high school   did matsuo put that idea in your head  even in death  he s still impeding me   why would someone like you veer off your path  you were taught from the very beginning that there was no point learning unnecessary things   utter nonsense  the only path in this world is the one i prepared for you  you will one day surpass me  and become the person who guides japan into the future  why can t you understand that   it seems i can t get through to you   the white room has resumed operations  this time  my plans are perfect  nothing will get in the way  i m prepared to make up for lost time  son across the table  the whole scene is their first face to face in a year and a half  dead butler used as leverage  self immolation last month after the son s prospects were crushed  bows out with the principal  her nerves framed the visit  ruined a butler s reputation  a son s schooling and a family s future without raising his voice  treats the suicide as a report  views his son as property  speaks in corporate and white room absolutes  admits the sixteen year plan broke in one year  still claims the single prepared path  blank page  page number only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the drop-out demand<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.55–64<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits opposite the sweating principal in the office; delivers the prepared drop-out papers and the Matsuo leverage.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"matsuo.html\">Matsuo<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“How about you take a seat? I came all the way here to meet with you, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Friends? Don’t make me laugh. There’s no way you’re capable of making friends,”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Then I assume you’re going to do as I say. No need to discuss anything; I’m busy anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve prepared the documents necessary for you to drop out. I spoke to the principal about it. All I need is for you to say yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For you, that might be true. But I have my own reasons.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Parent? You’ve never recognized me as your parent before,”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The fact is that you’ve been behaving selfishly. I ordered you to remain on standby,”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re my property. A man may do as he wishes with his property. Whether I keep you alive or kill you is up to me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you wonder how Matsuo’s doing? The person who told you about this school and gave you the idea to enroll?”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hired him to manage you for a year in his capacity as a butler, but he chose to go against his employer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “An outrageous, unforgiveable act. Naturally, Matsuo had to be punished.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can probably guess what I’m about to say,”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But now he’s been expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Matsuo’s son was strong. Even though he was expelled from the school on which he’d pinned his hopes, his determination didn’t fade. He … bounced back and immediately tried to enroll in other schools. I did whatever was necessary to crush his attempts to advance. I made him give up. I did the same to Matsuo, too. I tarnished his reputation, leaving him unable to find a job. His son also lost his way, and is now unemployed,”<span class=\"pg\">p.60–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He begged me to leave the boy alone, and committed suicide last month by self-immolation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right now, his son’s working part-time, earning enough to live on and nothing else, with no guarantee of a future. No dreams. No hope. His family’s tragedy is your fault. The boy must surely bear a deep grudge against you. Even in death, he won’t forgive you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The man who took care of you, who saved you, has died. And you show no reaction whatsoever. If Matsuo could see you now, he’d be full of regret.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Matsuo’s death has already been recorded. If necessary, I can send for the papers confirming it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve changed quite a bit, Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What happened that year? What made you so determined to go to this school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t entirely understand, but it seems that I have no choice but to accept. I suppose that temporarily suspending the facility’s activity was a mistake. To think that a plan sixteen years in the making could be ruined in just a year…”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand why you’re here,”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if you think the matter is settled, you’re naïve. As with Matsuo’s son, I can force you to quit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a statement made without proof.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no need to bring a bodyguard along to visit a high school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did Matsuo put that idea in your head? Even in death, he’s still impeding me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why would someone like you veer off your path? You were taught from the very beginning that there was no point learning unnecessary things.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Utter nonsense. The only path in this world is the one I prepared for you. You will one day surpass me, and become the person who guides Japan into the future. Why can’t you understand that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems I can’t get through to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The White Room has resumed operations. This time, my plans are perfect. Nothing will get in the way. I’m prepared to make up for lost time,”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Son across the table; the whole scene is their first face-to-face in a year and a half.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsuo<\/b> Dead butler used as leverage; self-immolation last month after the son’s prospects were crushed.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Bows out with the principal; her nerves framed the visit.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Ruined a butler’s reputation, a son’s schooling and a family’s future without raising his voice; treats the suicide as a report.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Views his son as property; speaks in corporate and White Room absolutes; admits the sixteen-year plan broke in one year; still claims the single prepared path.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank page (page number only).<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p65-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the ultimatum answered<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p65-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi ch 3  the ultimatum answered gets the free will refusal  watches sakayanagi block the expulsion on autonomy and tuition rules  and leaves without a card left   am i to assume a parent can t lie to their own child   you have no plans to return   how foolish  this school s nothing more than a barn full of common rabble  i m sure that your own class holds many such worthless bottomfeeders with no hope of salvation   you think that even incompetent morons can stand toe to toe with geniuses   you want to destroy my ideals  then   we should end this  we know that  no matter how long we talk  we ll never agree   that s right  since it s what his parent wishes  the school must immediately take appropriate action   you ve changed  too  where did the old  agreeable you go   you re free to succeed your father and carry on his wishes  however  if that s your intention  then why did you allow kiyotaka to enter this school   don t dodge the question  this school s fundamentally unlike ordinary schools  kiyotaka should never have been a suitable candidate for admission  i know that the interviews and exam are just for show   kiyotaka never should ve been among the possible candidates in the first place  it s abnormal that you didn t disqualify him   don t screw with me   if that s how things stand  i ll find another way   i understand  i haven t the slightest intention of putting any pressure on you   in that case  we re done talking  if you ll please excuse me   when will we meet again   coming to a place like this once is quite enough  free will answer  parting jab about visiting the school again ignored  chairman sakayanagi  father  blocks him on autonomy and government fees  nostalgia for the old agreeable days  falls back to  find another way  and rule compliant expulsion once the three way talk offer lands  ideologue about genius and rabble  admits no pressure while implying force  leaves rather than argue with the board","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the ultimatum answered<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.65–68<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gets the free-will refusal, watches Sakayanagi block the expulsion on autonomy and tuition rules, and leaves without a card left.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Am I to assume a parent can’t lie to their own child?”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You have no plans to return?”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How foolish. This school’s nothing more than a barn full of common rabble. I’m sure that your own class holds many such worthless bottomfeeders with no hope of salvation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You think that even incompetent morons can stand toe-to-toe with geniuses?”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You want to destroy my ideals, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We should end this. We know that, no matter how long we talk, we’ll never agree.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. Since it’s what his parent wishes, the school must immediately take appropriate action.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve changed, too. Where did the old, agreeable you go?”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re free to succeed your father and carry on his wishes. However, if that’s your intention, then why did you allow Kiyotaka to enter this school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t dodge the question. This school’s fundamentally unlike ordinary schools. Kiyotaka should never have been a suitable candidate for admission. I know that the interviews and exam are just for show,”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kiyotaka never should’ve been among the possible candidates in the first place. It’s abnormal that you didn’t disqualify him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t screw with me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that’s how things stand, I’ll find another way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand. I haven’t the slightest intention of putting any pressure on you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, we’re done talking. If you’ll please excuse me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When will we meet again?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Coming to a place like this once is quite enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Free-will answer; parting jab about visiting the school again ignored.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Chairman Sakayanagi (father) blocks him on autonomy and government fees; nostalgia for the old agreeable days.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Falls back to “find another way” and rule-compliant expulsion once the three-way-talk offer lands.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ideologue about genius and rabble; admits no pressure while implying force; leaves rather than argue with the board.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p55-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the drop-out demand<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v2-p6-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v2-p6-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.6-354<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v3-p7-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v3-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.7-368<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v4-p5-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v4-p5-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.5-284<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v4_5-p10-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v4_5-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.10-290<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v5-p7-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v5-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.7-243<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v6-p11-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v6-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.11-346<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v7-p7-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v7-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.7-207<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v8-p11-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v8-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.11-208<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v9-p8-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v9-p8-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.8-225<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v9_5-p10-1","v":"y2v9.5","y":2,"o":26,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v9_5-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9.5 · p.10-219<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v9_75-p4-1","v":"y2v9.75","y":2,"o":27,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v9_75-p4-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9.75 · p.4-8<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v10-p9-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v10-p9-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.9-235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v10_25-p1-1","v":"y2v10.25","y":2,"o":29,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v10_25-p1-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10.25 · p.1-10<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v11-p11-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v11-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.11-223<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v12_5-p107-1","v":"y2v12.5","y":2,"o":32,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi ch 7 mentioned appears in ch 7  appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v12_5-p107-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12.5 · p.107-121<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mentioned/appears in Ch.7.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Appears in this volume.<span class=\"pg\">p.107-121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p10-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi a life carved out of disparity and ambition atsuomi reflects on his origins in his own monologue   born poor  uneducated and in the countryside  with nothing but youth and an  indefinitely expanding ambition   rich  poor the disparity of wealth   this japan is a society of disparities   while i understood that principle  i possessed nothing   i was born in the countryside  extremely poor  and so uneducated it was pitiful   it was an indefinitely expanding  ambition one that couldn t be suppressed   i will definitely rise and stand at the pinnacle of this country  defines himself by disparity and a single  suppressless ambition to reach the pinnacle of the country   the only support he had in life  frames the whole volume as his monologue looking back on the path that led to the white room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">A life carved out of disparity and ambition<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.10–11<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Atsuomi reflects on his origins in his own monologue — born poor, uneducated and in the countryside, with nothing but youth and an &quot;indefinitely expanding ambition.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;RICH, POOR—THE DISPARITY of wealth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;This Japan is a society of disparities.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;While I understood that principle, I possessed nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I was born in the countryside, extremely poor, and so uneducated it was pitiful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;It was an indefinitely expanding &#x27;ambition&#x27;—one that couldn&#x27;t be suppressed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I will definitely rise and stand at the pinnacle of this country.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Defines himself by disparity and a single, suppressless ambition to reach the pinnacle of the country — the only support he had in life.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Frames the whole volume as his monologue looking back on the path that led to the White Room.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p11-1\">→ After: The failed election and the backroom rise<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p11-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"naoe-sensei ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the failed election and the backroom rise  at twenty five  i gained my first right to be elected   it was a fleeting  foolish dream  i underestimated the election and was miserably defeated   what was important in winning an election was which organization you belonged to and whom you followed   i requested to join the ruling  citizens  party  and began my steps as a politician   i took on the dirty backroom jobs that nobody wanted to do   eventually  as a secret blade for  naoe sensei  who controlled many factions within the citizens  party  i unhesitatingly delved into any wrongdoing facilitating underage girls  giving bribes  and committing espionage against rival organizations   at the age of thirty six  i had one foot in the realm of power  pragmatic and utterly unscrupulous   learns that power  not ideals  wins elections and becomes naoe sensei s  secret blade  committing any wrongdoing for advancement  becomes his secret blade  regards him as a stepping stone to be eventually surpassed and crushed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The failed election and the backroom rise<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.11–12<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;At twenty-five, I gained my first right to be elected.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;It was a fleeting, foolish dream. I underestimated the election and was miserably defeated.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;What was important in winning an election was which organization you belonged to and whom you followed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I requested to join the ruling &#x27;Citizens&#x27; Party&#x27; and began my steps as a politician.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I took on the dirty backroom jobs that nobody wanted to do.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Eventually, as a secret blade for &#x27;Naoe-sensei,&#x27; who controlled many factions within the Citizens&#x27; Party, I unhesitatingly delved into any wrongdoing—facilitating underage girls, giving bribes, and committing espionage against rival organizations.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;At the age of thirty-six, I had one foot in the realm of power.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pragmatic and utterly unscrupulous — learns that power, not ideals, wins elections and becomes Naoe-sensei&#x27;s &quot;secret blade,&quot; committing any wrongdoing for advancement.<span class=\"pg\">p.11–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Becomes his secret blade; regards him as a stepping stone to be eventually surpassed and crushed.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p10-1\">← Before: A life carved out of disparity and ambition<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p12-1\">→ After: The newborn and the White Room&#x27;s fourth phase<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p12-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"tabuchi ayanokouji-kiyotaka ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the newborn and the white room s fourth phase his child is born  he views the newborn with no emotion beyond relief at the political lever it represents   a newborn arrived  just one month old   no special emotions arose not a single one   if anything  i was relieved that the key to moving the higher ups had arrived   there are currently no issues  there were no problems found in various tests  including the brain waves    tabuchi s report  like the previous children  start the experiment immediately  coldly instrumental   sees his own son as a  key to moving the higher ups  feels nothing  and orders the experiment to begin at once  tabuchi runs the health dna tests and reports the results  atsuomi orders him to start the experiment  his newborn son  immediately entered into the white room experiment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The newborn and the White Room&#x27;s fourth phase<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.12–13<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">His child is born; he views the newborn with no emotion beyond relief at the political lever it represents.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#tabuchi\">Tabuchi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;A newborn arrived, just one month old.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;No special emotions arose—not a single one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;If anything, I was relieved that the key to moving the higher-ups had arrived.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;There are currently no issues. There were no problems found in various tests, including the brain waves.&quot; — Tabuchi&#x27;s report<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;Like the previous children, start the experiment immediately.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coldly instrumental — sees his own son as a &quot;key to moving the higher-ups,&quot; feels nothing, and orders the experiment to begin at once.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tabuchi<\/b> Tabuchi runs the health/DNA tests and reports the results; Atsuomi orders him to start the experiment.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His newborn son, immediately entered into the White Room experiment.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p11-1\">← Before: The failed election and the backroom rise<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p15-1\">→ After: The staged goodbye and the vow to reach the top<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p15-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakayanagi tabuchi naoe-sensei ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the staged goodbye and the vow to reach the top holds his son through the glass before the white room  staging an emotional farewell for the cameras   this child is more important than my own life  and i m sending him to the white room  capture the determination and tension on camera   a parent who s indifferent about leaving their child  and a parent who reluctantly entrusts their child for the future   anyway  all the necessary preparations are now complete  connect me to sakayanagi   i would use anything  even my own child  discard it  and reach the top   even someone with absolute authority  like naoe sensei  was no different as a stepping stone   if you don t want to die  you better struggle on your own  kiyotaka   the turning point came about four years after i started working under naoe sensei  calculated and ruthless   stages a reluctant father image for fundraising  treats his child and naoe sensei alike as disposable stepping stones  and addresses kiyotaka with a parting challenge to survive alone  sends him to the white room as the fourth phase subject  tells him he must struggle on his own  requests to be connected to him once preparations are complete  directs him to capture the staged farewell on camera  resolves to eventually surpass and crush him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The staged goodbye and the vow to reach the top<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.15–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Holds his son through the glass before the White Room, staging an emotional farewell for the cameras.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#tabuchi\">Tabuchi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;This child is more important than my own life, and I&#x27;m sending him to the White Room. Capture the determination and tension on camera.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;A parent who&#x27;s indifferent about leaving their child, and a parent who reluctantly entrusts their child for the future.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Anyway, all the necessary preparations are now complete. Connect me to Sakayanagi.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I would use anything, even my own child, discard it, and reach the top.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Even someone with absolute authority, like Naoe-sensei, was no different as a stepping stone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;If you don&#x27;t want to die, you better struggle on your own, Kiyotaka.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;The turning point came about four years after I started working under Naoe-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calculated and ruthless — stages a reluctant-father image for fundraising, treats his child and Naoe-sensei alike as disposable stepping stones, and addresses Kiyotaka with a parting challenge to survive alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Sends him to the White Room as the fourth-phase subject; tells him he must struggle on his own.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">sakayanagi<\/b> Requests to be connected to him once preparations are complete.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tabuchi<\/b> Directs him to capture the staged farewell on camera.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Resolves to eventually surpass and crush him.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p12-1\">← Before: The newborn and the White Room&#x27;s fourth phase<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p17-1\">→ After: Waiting for Naoe-sensei; on Kamogawa<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p17-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"kamogawa naoe-sensei ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi waiting for naoe sensei  on kamogawa waits an hour in the freezing cold outside ryoutei sasagawa for naoe sensei  with kamogawa   it s always like this  for naoe sensei  the appointed time is merely a guideline   you re naive  we re lucky if he comes here today at all  oftentimes  he doesn t even show up   even being late is a weapon for naoe sensei  like the anecdote of miyamoto musashi at ganryujima   it would be troublesome if you look down on naoe sensei i ll just dismiss them like that   they say that seeking hardship is good  even if you have to pay for it  but i ve been hit once or twice  patient  loyal and world weary   treats naoe s lateness as deliberate power  absorbs the anger of those kept waiting  and despises the spoiled second generation politicians  manages and lectures the complaining rookie  sees him as a leech who wants only to survive  serves as his intermediary and shielding face  absorbing resentment so naoe never has to","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Waiting for Naoe-sensei; on Kamogawa<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.17–19<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits an hour in the freezing cold outside Ryoutei Sasagawa for Naoe-sensei, with Kamogawa.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;It&#x27;s always like this. For Naoe-sensei, the appointed time is merely a guideline.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;You&#x27;re naive. We&#x27;re lucky if he comes here today at all. Oftentimes, he doesn&#x27;t even show up.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Even being late is a weapon for Naoe-sensei. Like the anecdote of Miyamoto Musashi at Ganryujima.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;It would be troublesome if you look down on Naoe-sensei—I&#x27;ll just dismiss them like that.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;They say that seeking hardship is good, even if you have to pay for it, but I&#x27;ve been hit once or twice.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Patient, loyal and world-weary — treats Naoe&#x27;s lateness as deliberate power, absorbs the anger of those kept waiting, and despises the spoiled second-generation politicians.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Manages and lectures the complaining rookie; sees him as a leech who wants only to survive.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Serves as his intermediary and shielding face, absorbing resentment so Naoe never has to.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p15-1\">← Before: The staged goodbye and the vow to reach the top<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p20-1\">→ After: Naoe arrives; the meeting with Asama<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p20-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"asama kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi naoe arrives  the meeting with asama naoe s taxi arrives  atsuomi stops kamogawa from reacting rashly when a woman is seen with him   don t do anything rash   good work today  naoe sensei   where is asama   he s been waiting  i ll guide you   asama sensei  i ve brought naoe sensei  refuses the temptation to eavesdrop on the two major politicians   scheming would be exposed and end his career  vigilant and disciplined   shields naoe from embarrassment  reads the room  and withdraws rather than risk the  devil s  temptation to gather information  guides naoe to the waiting asama hisashi  notes the instant master servant role reversal  signals him to pay the fare and keeps him in line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Naoe arrives; the meeting with Asama<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.20–23<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Naoe&#x27;s taxi arrives; Atsuomi stops Kamogawa from reacting rashly when a woman is seen with him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#asama\">Asama<\/a> · <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Don&#x27;t do anything rash.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Good work today, Naoe-sensei.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Where is Asama?&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;He&#x27;s been waiting. I&#x27;ll guide you.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;Asama-sensei, I&#x27;ve brought Naoe-sensei.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Refuses the temptation to eavesdrop on the two major politicians — scheming would be exposed and end his career.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Vigilant and disciplined — shields Naoe from embarrassment, reads the room, and withdraws rather than risk the &quot;devil&#x27;s&quot; temptation to gather information.<span class=\"pg\">p.20–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asama<\/b> Guides Naoe to the waiting Asama Hisashi; notes the instant master-servant role reversal.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Signals him to pay the fare and keeps him in line.<span class=\"pg\">p.20–21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p17-1\">← Before: Waiting for Naoe-sensei; on Kamogawa<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p24-1\">→ After: The private room: seiza and the sake<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p24-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the private room  seiza and the sake in a separate private room with kamogawa  warns him not to drink the ceremonial sake   don t drink the sake   are you planning to send off naoe sensei with the smell of alcohol  this is nothing more than a formality   it s a habit  in front of naoe sensei and the others  i have to sit in seiza for hours without any trouble  abstains from sake after witnessing a predecessor erased for it  and keeps himself in seiza always so formal occasions cost him nothing  teaches him the room s unspoken rules","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The private room: seiza and the sake<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.24–26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In a separate private room with Kamogawa, warns him not to drink the ceremonial sake.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Don&#x27;t drink the sake.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Are you planning to send off Naoe-sensei with the smell of alcohol? This is nothing more than a formality.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;It&#x27;s a habit. In front of Naoe-sensei and the others, I have to sit in seiza for hours without any trouble.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Abstains from sake after witnessing a predecessor erased for it, and keeps himself in seiza always so formal occasions cost him nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Teaches him the room&#x27;s unspoken rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p20-1\">← Before: Naoe arrives; the meeting with Asama<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p27-1\">→ After: Naoe&#x27;s summons: Kijima and the project envelope<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p27-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"naoe-sensei kijima isomaru ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi naoe s summons  kijima and the project envelope summoned by naoe after the meeting to another private room  with kijima s untouched cups evident   this is my fourth year studying under you  sensei   i m truly thankful  naoe sensei  you picked up someone like me   i believe he has many achievements  but if there s something to highlight  it would be  anhs   you must be joking  whether it s the present or future  the only person i will learn from is you  naoe sensei  carefully deferential   deflects naoe s praise  declares loyalty  and correctly identifies kijima s anhs as his rise  views him as the  have not  who rose fastest  naoe probes his loyalty and hints at a new project  identified by naoe as the greatest enemy  a young  clean  spotlight politician rising on anhs  naoe s rival  the third ranking party figure   old fashioned and straightforward","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Naoe&#x27;s summons: Kijima and the project envelope<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.27–30<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Summoned by Naoe after the meeting to another private room, with Kijima&#x27;s untouched cups evident.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kijima.html\">Kijima<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#isomaru\">Isomaru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;This is my fourth year studying under you, Sensei.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;I&#x27;m truly thankful, Naoe-sensei. You picked up someone like me.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;I believe he has many achievements, but if there&#x27;s something to highlight, it would be &#x27;ANHS&#x27;.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;You must be joking. Whether it&#x27;s the present or future, the only person I will learn from is you, Naoe-sensei.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Carefully deferential — deflects Naoe&#x27;s praise, declares loyalty, and correctly identifies Kijima&#x27;s ANHS as his rise.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Views him as the &quot;have-not&quot; who rose fastest; Naoe probes his loyalty and hints at a new project.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kijima<\/b> Identified by Naoe as the greatest enemy; a young, clean, spotlight politician rising on ANHS.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Isomaru<\/b> Naoe&#x27;s rival, the third-ranking party figure — old-fashioned and straightforward.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p24-1\">← Before: The private room: seiza and the sake<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p31-1\">→ After: &quot;What makes a politician outstanding&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p31-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"naoe-sensei kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi  what makes a politician outstanding  naoe poses a drinking game question to kamogawa and atsuomi   although i m inexperienced  i think of someone like you  naoe sensei   a bad politician serves tempura to a customer who wants sushi   a customer is a customer  sometimes they are the citizens  sometimes they are politicians  and sometimes they are something else altogether   a good politician serves delicious sushi to a customer who wants sushi  probably  only about thirty percent  no  maybe only twenty percent of politicians can do this   if you re going to call a politician  exceptionally outstanding  more is required  even if a customer wants sushi  they can guide them to be fully satisfied with curry or beef bowl   when i had just started studying under you  naoe sensei  you once told me that people s actions are determined by their goals   i will devote my whole heart and soul to this task  articulate and ambitious   defines a truly outstanding politician as one who can redirect desire to a satisfying alternative  then accepts naoe s envelope project with a bow  knowing failure would ash his four years  challenges and delights him with the sushi metaphor  accepts the envelope project that promises fame  watches him give a simplistic answer about responding to the citizens  wishes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p31-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">&quot;What makes a politician outstanding&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.31–33<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Naoe poses a drinking-game question to Kamogawa and Atsuomi.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Although I&#x27;m inexperienced, I think of someone like you, Naoe-sensei.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;A bad politician serves tempura to a customer who wants sushi.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;A customer is a customer. Sometimes they are the citizens, sometimes they are politicians, and sometimes they are something else altogether.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;A good politician serves delicious sushi to a customer who wants sushi. Probably, only about thirty percent... no, maybe only twenty percent of politicians can do this.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;If you&#x27;re going to call a politician &#x27;exceptionally outstanding,&#x27; more is required. Even if a customer wants sushi, they can guide them to be fully satisfied with curry or beef bowl.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;When I had just started studying under you, Naoe-sensei, you once told me that people&#x27;s actions are determined by their goals.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I will devote my whole heart and soul to this task.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Articulate and ambitious — defines a truly outstanding politician as one who can redirect desire to a satisfying alternative, then accepts Naoe&#x27;s envelope project with a bow, knowing failure would ash his four years.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Challenges and delights him with the sushi metaphor; accepts the envelope project that promises fame.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Watches him give a simplistic answer about responding to the citizens&#x27; wishes.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p27-1\">← Before: Naoe&#x27;s summons: Kijima and the project envelope<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p42-1\">→ After: Planning the Human Resource Development Project; using Kamogawa<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p42-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"kamogawa ooba naoe-sensei ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi planning the human resource development project  using kamogawa at his cluttered office  plans the  human resource development project    gathering newborns and securing a huge budget   this project is going to be troublesome   it s me  put ooba on  i have a new job for him   kamogawa  i m telling you this for your own good  don t mimic the likes of kisarazu   i m not saying don t buy real estate  i m just saying don t miss the right timing  money is finite  but it holds infinite possibilities   can you be of use   for the project in question  it s essential to secure an experimental facility  i ll leave the location selection to you   from a budgetary perspective  seems like it ll inevitably be in the countryside   there are more than a few construction companies that would have its dirt revealed when dug into  ruthlessly pragmatic   uses whatever pieces work regardless of morality  contacts the criminal ooba group to acquire newborns  and manipulates kamogawa with small praise into useful service  puts him to work selecting a facility location and securing funding  knows a little praise makes him useful  contacts him about acquiring newborns   evil means are unavoidable  notes naoe could make funds appear with one word  since he can t  a major investor is urgently needed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p42-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Planning the Human Resource Development Project; using Kamogawa<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.42–47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At his cluttered office, plans the &quot;Human Resource Development Project&quot; — gathering newborns and securing a huge budget.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ooba\">Ooba<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;…This project is going to be troublesome.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;It&#x27;s me. Put Ooba on. I have a new job for him.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Kamogawa. I&#x27;m telling you this for your own good, don&#x27;t mimic the likes of Kisarazu.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I&#x27;m not saying don&#x27;t buy real estate. I&#x27;m just saying don&#x27;t miss the right timing. Money is finite, but it holds infinite possibilities.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;Can you be of use?&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;For the project in question, it&#x27;s essential to secure an experimental facility. I&#x27;ll leave the location selection to you.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;From a budgetary perspective, seems like it&#x27;ll inevitably be in the countryside.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;There are more than a few construction companies that would have its dirt revealed when dug into.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ruthlessly pragmatic — uses whatever pieces work regardless of morality, contacts the criminal Ooba group to acquire newborns, and manipulates Kamogawa with small praise into useful service.<span class=\"pg\">p.42–47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Puts him to work selecting a facility location and securing funding; knows a little praise makes him useful.<span class=\"pg\">p.42–47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ooba<\/b> Contacts him about acquiring newborns — evil means are unavoidable.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Notes Naoe could make funds appear with one word; since he can&#x27;t, a major investor is urgently needed.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p31-1\">← Before: &quot;What makes a politician outstanding&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p48-1\">→ After: Visiting Sakayanagi Narimori for funding<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p48-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi visiting sakayanagi narimori for funding visits the sakayanagi mansion in shirokane to ask for help funding the project   nice to meet you  my name is ayanokouji  thank you for making time in your busy schedule   i recalled naoe sensei saying that if i ever had a problem  i could rely on you  sakayanagi san that s why i ve come to visit  sakayanagi narimori  arisu s father  receives him   slender  gentle  feigning humility  he says naoe spoke highly of ayanokouji and that they are the same age  his own lines are recorded on his own card  confident but mannerly   chooses to sit without making himself small  while knowing he is the one asking a favor","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Visiting Sakayanagi Narimori for funding<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.48–49<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Visits the Sakayanagi mansion in Shirokane to ask for help funding the project.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Nice to meet you. My name is Ayanokouji. Thank you for making time in your busy schedule.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;I recalled Naoe-sensei saying that if I ever had a problem, I could rely on you, Sakayanagi-san—that&#x27;s why I&#x27;ve come to visit.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakayanagi Narimori (Arisu&#x27;s father) receives him — slender, gentle, feigning humility. He says Naoe spoke highly of Ayanokouji and that they are the same age. His own lines are recorded on his own card.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Confident but mannerly — chooses to sit without making himself small, while knowing he is the one asking a favor.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p42-1\">← Before: Planning the Human Resource Development Project; using Kamogawa<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p70-1\">→ After: The White Room facility named; the mentor&#x27;s warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p70-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the white room facility named  the mentor s warning reviews photos of the finished facility in saitama  kamogawa reports construction complete   we ll call it white room  we want to emphasize white s purity in the image   there are more than a few construction companies that would have its dirt revealed when dug into   kamogawa  i need to teach you something important  the world of politics isn t just about friends or foes   never mind  it seems it was too soon for you  sees the  white room  name as image strategy  knows he walks a bridge that could collapse and tries  in vain  to warn the naive kamogawa  credits him for moving the financial world  judges him not yet ready to understand political danger","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p70-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The White Room facility named; the mentor&#x27;s warning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.70–71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reviews photos of the finished facility in Saitama; Kamogawa reports construction complete.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;We&#x27;ll call it White Room. We want to emphasize white&#x27;s purity in the image.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;There are more than a few construction companies that would have its dirt revealed when dug into.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Kamogawa, I need to teach you something important. The world of politics isn&#x27;t just about friends or foes.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;Never mind. It seems it was too soon for you.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sees the &quot;White Room&quot; name as image strategy; knows he walks a bridge that could collapse and tries (in vain) to warn the naive Kamogawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Credits him for moving the financial world; judges him not yet ready to understand political danger.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p48-1\">← Before: Visiting Sakayanagi Narimori for funding<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p72-1\">→ After: Hiring Souya and the other &quot;problem&quot; experts<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p72-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"souya kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi hiring souya and the other  problem  experts interviews souya  a disgraced former doctor  for the research lab   i haven t told you that you re hired yet   i don t care about your career   which university you graduated from  which hospital you worked at  what crimes you ve committed i have no interest in any of that   i m only interested in your current thoughts and abilities   i ll give you a chance to resurrect yourself   he has no close associates around him  he s obsessed with money and doesn t seek honor from the outside world   we ll let the people we hire compete  then  the answers will naturally emerge  coldly exploitative   hires competent outcasts who can be paid and controlled  pits experts against each other to reveal ability  and fires without mercy if results disappoint  hires him on the spot as a researcher former doctor to manage the subjects  lets him observe  dismisses his worries about hiring such people","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Hiring Souya and the other &quot;problem&quot; experts<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.72–75<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Interviews Souya, a disgraced former doctor, for the research lab.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#souya\">Sōya<\/a> · <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;I haven&#x27;t told you that you&#x27;re hired yet.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;I don&#x27;t care about your career.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Which university you graduated from, which hospital you worked at, what crimes you&#x27;ve committed—I have no interest in any of that.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I&#x27;m only interested in your current thoughts and abilities.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I&#x27;ll give you a chance to resurrect yourself.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;He has no close associates around him. He&#x27;s obsessed with money and doesn&#x27;t seek honor from the outside world.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;We&#x27;ll let the people we hire compete. Then, the answers will naturally emerge.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coldly exploitative — hires competent outcasts who can be paid and controlled, pits experts against each other to reveal ability, and fires without mercy if results disappoint.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sōya<\/b> Hires him on the spot as a researcher/former doctor to manage the subjects.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Lets him observe; dismisses his worries about hiring such people.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p70-1\">← Before: The White Room facility named; the mentor&#x27;s warning<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p76-1\">→ After: Tsukishiro: the journalist&#x27;s body and the background check<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p76-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"tsukishiro naoe-sensei ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi tsukishiro  the journalist s body and the background check finds tsukishiro s business card on the floor after the interviews  arranges to meet him   then we ll get things started now  i won t let you say it s impossible   you bastard   that isn t it  huh  you re probably just keeping an eye on a politician to replace me   i don t care about that  what i want to know is whether you were impersonating naoe sensei when this journalist met you at the restaurant   at least i wouldn t be foolish enough to allow the body to be found   there are many things i dislike about this  but you can t make an omelet without breaking eggs    corpus reads  you can t make an omelet   i understand  how much   it was a dugout shed used to store agricultural tools managed by the neighborhood adults  realizes the journalist s body was intentionally left found   to chill the  rats  watching naoe  with an unknown scapegoat set to take the blame  unfazed by a possible killer   feels anger rather than fear  reads tsukishiro s strategy  and agrees to work with him while calmly disclosing his deprived childhood  meets him  recognizes him as naoe s observer cleanup man and supporter  and decides to use him to recruit personnel  realizes naoe had tsukishiro watching insuring the project from the start","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p76-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Tsukishiro: the journalist&#x27;s body and the background check<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.76–84<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Finds Tsukishiro&#x27;s business card on the floor after the interviews; arranges to meet him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Then we&#x27;ll get things started now. I won&#x27;t let you say it&#x27;s impossible.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;…You bastard.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;That isn&#x27;t it, huh? You&#x27;re probably just keeping an eye on a politician to replace me.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I don&#x27;t care about that. What I want to know is whether you were impersonating Naoe-sensei when this journalist met you at the restaurant.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;At least I wouldn&#x27;t be foolish enough to allow the body to be found.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;There are many things I dislike about this, but you can&#x27;t make an omelet without breaking eggs.&#x27;&quot; — corpus reads &quot;you can&#x27;t make an omelet&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I understand. How much?&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;It was a dugout shed used to store agricultural tools managed by the neighborhood adults.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes the journalist&#x27;s body was intentionally left found — to chill the &quot;rats&quot; watching Naoe, with an unknown scapegoat set to take the blame.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Unfazed by a possible killer — feels anger rather than fear, reads Tsukishiro&#x27;s strategy, and agrees to work with him while calmly disclosing his deprived childhood.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Meets him; recognizes him as Naoe&#x27;s observer/cleanup man and supporter, and decides to use him to recruit personnel.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Realizes Naoe had Tsukishiro watching/insuring the project from the start.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p72-1\">← Before: Hiring Souya and the other &quot;problem&quot; experts<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
